%N A402583 Compute otherwise like A328571, but take the exponents e from the prime factorization of n; denominators of fractions whose numerators are given by A402582.
%H A402583 Antti Karttunen, <a href="/A402583/b402583.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..16170</a>
%H A402583 <a href="/index/Pri#primorialbase">Index entries for sequences related to primorial base</a>.
%o A402583 (PARI) A402583(n) = { my(orgn=n,s=0, p=2); while(n, s += (valuation(orgn,p)/p); n = n\p; p = nextprime(1+p)); denominator(s); };
%Y A402583 Cf. A402582 (numerators).
%Y A402583 Cf. also A083345, A328571, A402581.
%K A402583 nonn,easy,frac,new
